decisions:
  - id: three_separate_skills
    summary: loop-engineering-advisory, specialist-recruitment-advisory, context-hygiene-advisory are three focused skills, not one unified skill, matching existing coordination skill granularity
  - id: loop_state_disk_persisted
    summary: loop-engineering fallback tracks iteration state in an optional HANDOFF.toon loop_state block so it survives context resets, session restarts, or model/provider swaps mid-loop
  - id: no_new_bin_scripts
    summary: all three skills are judgment/instruction skills like team-selection and agent-team-fallback; no new .agentic-template/bin/ command
  - id: presence_only_testing
    summary: validated by check-repo-contract presence + frontmatter checks only, no new self-test fixtures, matching how other coordination skills are tested
  - id: specialist_recruitment_vs_team_selection
    summary: specialist-recruitment-advisory is the earlier mid-task tripwire that surfaces an explicit offer; team-selection still owns the actual roster mechanics once accepted

risks:
  - advisory skills could become noisy if triggers are too broad; triggers are scoped narrowly (repeating pattern detected / specialist domain matched with none engaged / context growing or boundary reached)
  - loop_state block must be removed once a fallback loop completes, or it will look like stale abandoned work in HANDOFF.toon

files_changed:
  - docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-proactive-advisory-design.md (new, committed)
  - HANDOFF.toon

